# Keep the build context to the source that is actually served.
#
# This file does two jobs. The obvious one is speed: without it the context includes .git
# and 125 KB of design prose. The one that matters is that anything sent to the daemon
# can end up in an image layer by accident, so a local .env, a suggestions store or a
# tunnel token must never be in the context in the first place. The Dockerfile also names
# its COPYs explicitly, so this is the second of two independent reasons none of the
# below reaches the image.

.git
.gitignore

# Developer tooling. Not served, not imported by anything under server/.
tests
tools

# Long-form documentation. Read it in the repository, not in the image.
DESIGN.md
THREAT-MODEL.md
CLAUDE.md
docs

# The browser extension is a separate artefact with its own copies of the pages. The
# server only ever serves public/, so shipping it would put a second, divergent copy of
# app.html inside the image where nothing can reach it and everything can confuse it.
extension

# Deployment material. Nothing under deploy/ belongs in the image, least of all a compose
# file carrying an operator's own hostnames, EXCEPT the one script the docs tell you to
# run inside the container to read the suggestion box back.
#
# The exception line is not optional and its absence is not silent: excluding the
# directory without re-including that file makes the matching COPY in the Dockerfile fail
# the build with "not found". Measured, 2026-08-10, by writing it the other way first.
deploy
!deploy/read-suggestions.mjs

# Secrets and state. None of these should exist in a checkout, and if one does it must
# not be copied into a layer that gets pushed to a registry.
.env
.env.*
secrets
data
*.jsonl

# Anything a stray `npm install` left behind. Warp Gate has no dependencies; if this
# directory exists it is not part of the program.
node_modules
